referenceSolutions.java:
class Solution {
  public int branchNotebookThresholdFile(TreeNode root, int k) {
    TreeNode a=root; List<Integer> out=new ArrayList<>();
    {class Walk {void visit(TreeNode node){if(node==null)return;out.add(node.val);visit(node.left);visit(node.right);}}new Walk().visit(a);}
    int answer=0;for(int x:out)if(x>=k)answer++;return answer;
  }
}

privateData.editorialMd:
The working idea

Traverse the binary tree in root-left-right order and produce its node values. A missing root produces no values.

Return how many values in the derived sequence are at least k.

Why this works

Each derived value follows the unit's stated order and includes exactly the items allowed by its definition. The receipt then folds or filters those values without changing their meaning. Check the empty, singleton, repeated and maximum-size inputs before trusting the final total.

Target time O(n); space O(n).

